<p class=3D"byline">By Jane Reporter</p>
<p>Researchers announced today that reading aloud improves comprehension fo=
r many listeners.</p><p>The study followed two hundred participants over si=
x months and measured recall after each session.</p><p>Participants who lis=
tened while following the text remembered noticeably more than those who on=
ly read silently.</p><p>The authors caution that the effect varied widely b=
etween individuals and between kinds of material.</p>
